  <prompt>
    Author the `compose-explain-clause` capability as an Action row + Binding row (ADR-039), mirror-first under infra/dataverse/, dispatched through the shipped session-dispatch seam (NO new endpoint). The Action carries a plain-language clause-explanation SystemPrompt and a structured OutputSchemaJson `{explanation, keyConcepts[], relatedPlaybookIds[]}` (FR-07); the Binding is a Click-path, toolbar-invoked routing row consuming the `compose-selection` JPS scope. This is one of five R2 catalog rows; it reuses the prompt/schema pattern proven in Spike 1 and authors THROUGH the core's triple-twin hoisted description source (never a fourth hand-maintained twin). It ships with eval cases in task 045.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    AI platform developer fluent in JPS (JSON Prompt Schema) Action authoring, the ADR-039 Action+Binding catalog model, OutputSchemaJson / OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator constraints, and the redesign-r1 mirror-first catalog-governance workflow.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A deployable `compose-explain-clause` Action row (SystemPrompt + OutputSchemaJson + Temperature + ModelDeploymentId) and its Click-path Binding row, both authored mirror-first under infra/dataverse/ through the core's hoisted description source, consuming `compose-selection`, returning schema `{explanation: string, keyConcepts: string[], relatedPlaybookIds: string[]}` that passes OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator with no property-level boolean `required`. Dispatch adds zero new routes. Row is eval-ready for task 045 (does not merge without eval coverage).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Spec FR-07 + design §7 (R2 Catalog Roster row 2) + §7.4 (authoring pipeline, mirror-first, through the triple-twin hoist). One of five R2 Action+Binding pairs. Read action: selection → "Explain" in the BubbleMenu toolbar → schema-valid explanation streams into the Assistant; sources surface in the Context pane. No `compose` disposition (this is not an edit action). Consumes the `compose-selection` scope defined in R1, whose `description` field doubles as LLM behavioral guidance and toolbar tooltip (FR-23 / adeu "tool descriptions ARE the prompt").
